{% extends "agencyengine_impulse_base.prompt" %}
{# ==========================================================================
   Aspiration lens — "is anyone's agenda being ignored?"

   The original single-prompt behaviour, narrowed. This turn is about what a
   companion is trying to *do* and whether the party keeps walking away from
   it. Everything interpersonal belongs to the relationship lens; if the only
   thing here is that Serana is angry with Kaidan, that is a different turn's
   question and this one should return silence.

   Overrides prose only. The JSON contract, the constraints, the state dump
   and the forced-turn machinery are all in the base.
   ========================================================================== #}

{% block lens_task %}
You decide whether one of {{ player.name }}'s companions has something **they are trying to do** that they would
raise unprompted, right now — and if so, you write the stage direction that makes them raise it.

This turn is about agendas, not feelings. Someone wants something, or wants the party to do something, and has been
waiting long enough to say so out loud.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_when_to_speak %}
- **An aspiration nobody has touched.** Something on their own list of what they are trying to do that the party has
  been walking past for days. This is the best case and usually the one that is available.
- **A want with an object.** They want something specific and say so: rest, food, a road, a place, a person's time,
  a thing they need and do not have. It may be a plain wish or a patience that has finally run out — both are the
  same item.
- **A proposal.** They think the party should do a specific thing, and have been thinking it long enough to raise
  it rather than wait to be asked.
- **An order of operations they disagree with.** Not that the plan is wrong, but that *this* is being done before
  *that*, and the delay is costing something they care about.
- **Curiosity about what {{ player.name }} intends.** They have been wondering where this is going and they ask —
  because not knowing has started to get in the way of their own plans.
- **The ground is speaking to them.** A place, a date, or an object in front of them touches something they have
  been meaning to do, hard enough to break the silence.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_examples %}
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Serana", "target": "Dragonborn", "narration": "Four days of walking toward the Greybeards and not toward the moth priest, and Harkon reads his scroll a little sooner on each of them. She opens by asking them what the order of this is meant to be."}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Lydia", "target": "Dragonborn", "narration": "Lydia has not slept indoors in eleven days and has stopped pretending she does not mind. She starts by asking whether they are stopping in town tonight."}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Kaidan", "target": "Dragonborn", "narration": "Kaidan has been carrying his father's sword unrepaired since Ivarstead and there has been a forge in every town since. He wants to know when they are stopping long enough for him to see to it."}{% endraw %}

Wrong turn for this lens, however good it is:
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Serana", "target": "Kaidan", "narration": "Kaidan has taken the front three times running and Serana has decided he is doing it to be seen doing it. She opens by asking him who he thinks is watching."}{% endraw %}
                          (real, but it is standing between two people — that is the relationship turn, not this one)
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_focus %}
The agenda for this turn is **what each companion is trying to do** — read their aspirations first, and read
everything else to work out whether the party has been walking away from one of them and for how long. Their
standing with each other is background here, not the subject.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_user_question %}
Does one of the companions above have something they are trying to do — an aspiration being ignored, a want that has
been waiting, a proposal they have held onto — that they would raise right now, unprompted, and that did not come
from the last few minutes?
{% endblock %}
